From 8f15bbfb714825a32e7b6d3f15a387409edb9144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:34:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ceremony: errChanged for a file swapped after Lstat, path and
 remedy for ErrNotRegular, witnesses line before the rename
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backlog 93: lreadEntry refuses an entry that os.Lstat shows as no
regular file with store.ErrNotRegular, before it opens it (27A). A
regular file replaced after that os.Lstat by a FIFO, a directory or a
device with a driver was opened and refused with the same
store.ErrNotRegular, so the message was that of an entry that is no
regular file ("remove it by hand" in checkDataPlatform), not errChanged.
Now an open that finds no regular file is errChanged ("was replaced
before it was opened"); after any other error of the open the entry is
looked at again, and a link, an entry that is no regular file now (also
one that got the inode number of the removed file), another file or a
name gone by now is errChanged as well ("is gone" for the last).
store.ErrNotRegular is left for an entry that os.Lstat showed as no
regular file. The comments name the window left: what is put in place
of the regular file between os.Lstat and the open is opened where it
can be (O_RDONLY|O_NONBLOCK|O_NOCTTY), a device with a driver as well,
and a device node that exists on the same file system gets there
without CAP_MKNOD; for a socket the open is only tried. New test hook
"<at>-failed <name>" after a failed open; its error stands for a failing
second os.Lstat.

Backlog 94: store.ErrNotRegular of readEntry in runPublish (witnesses.rec
with and without ReplaceWitnesses, the comparison with the export,
freeName, the succession succChain.need would relog, and the branch
"written meanwhile") is completed by notRegularErr with the path, the
kinds, "nothing written or logged" and the remedy of checkDataPlatform;
in the branch "written meanwhile" it says instead that nothing is logged
and other files of the export may be written already.
errors.Is(err, store.ErrNotRegular) stays true; readEntry's own error is
unchanged.

Backlog 85: PublishOptions.WitnessesReplacing (a callback, no new
command-line option) is called after the export's files are written,
before the temporary file is written and renamed over witnesses.rec
with ReplaceWitnesses, when WitnessesReplaced or WitnessesLinkReplaced
follows the rename; gomail-ceremony publish prints a line
"platform/witnesses.rec wird jetzt ersetzt: ..." (or "... ist ein
symbolischer Link und wird jetzt ... ersetzt: ...") ending in "fehlt die
nächste Zeile, platform/witnesses.rec selbst ansehen." before the line it
prints after the rename, which is unchanged. A publish killed between
the rename and that line (SIGKILL) has printed the first one. When the
temporary file or the rename fails after that line, the error names
witnesses.rec, says that it is unchanged (every error of
store.ReplaceFileIn leaves it so; the fsync of platform/ after the
rename is not part of it), that nothing is logged and that files of the
export may be written already, and gives the remedy: run the same
publish again. No file format changes.

Backlog 95, tests: TestPublishMeanwhileSameContent (written meanwhile
with the export's content is not counted as written, mutant A11/W4),
TestPublishDeviceAtLstatNeverOpened (inotify IN_OPEN on platform/; the
device 0:0 needs no CAP_MKNOD, so mutant Y1 fails without root as
well), listDir shows a directory that shows nothing below it as
"<path>/", so platformSnapshot sees a directory under a name
(TestListDir). Further tests: TestPublishEntrySwappedAfterLstat,
TestPublishEntryGoneAfterFailedOpen, TestPublishEntryBackAfterNotRegularOpen
(the file back after a FIFO failed the open), TestPublishEntryInodeReused
(a socket or the device 0:0 with the inode number of the removed file),
TestPublishEMFILEAtOpen (RLIMIT_NOFILE 0 at the open, also with a
failing second os.Lstat; no root needed), TestPublishNotRegularWrapped,
TestPublishWitnessesAnnouncedBeforeKill (regular file, symbolic and
hard link; child killed with SIGKILL right after the rename),
TestPublishReplacingAfterExportFiles, TestPublishReplaceFailsAfterLine,
TestReplacingText; the expected output of the publish tests of the
command line has the new line.

No file format, signed record, signature domain or check rule of the
clients changes.

Task: docs/tasks/28-nach-m1-nacht2c.md (Paket 28A)
